2026-10-16 14:08:40,080 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=Black ice is a type of ice that forms when snow falls onto hard surfaces like concrete, asphalt, or even metal. Black ice is very slippery and can cause accidents if not treated properly.
If you are driving and there is black ice on the road, your first priority should be to slow down your speed as much as possible. This will help reduce the risk of accidents caused by black ice.
Once you have slowed down your speed as much as possible, your next priority should be to try to avoid driving over or onto black ice. If it is not possible to avoid driving over or onto black ice, then you should continue driving at a slower speed and try to avoid any potential accidents caused by black ice.
