he exercise. Then, set \nyour parking brake, shift to neutral/park, and sound \nyour horn. This will inform the examiner you have \ncompleted the exercise. (See Figure 12.3 on page \n12-4)  \n12.2.4  \nExercise 4 – Reverse Offset Backing \nYou will demonstrate your ability to offset back and \npark a vehicle at the end of an alley. From the \nstopped position of the previous exercise and \nparallel with the outer bounda\n\n[5] Question: DL-7C\nExcerpt: 14-3\nON EVERY TRUCK OR BUS LESS THAN 80” IN WIDTH  \n(Front, Rear, Side) \nON EVERY TRUCK OR BUS 80” OR MORE IN WIDTH  \n(Front, Rear, Side) \nON EACH SIDE \nVehicle Lighting and Reflector Requirements\n</sources>\nQuestion: What is the minimum depth of tread on front wheels"}], "stream": true, "options": {"temperature": 0.2, "num_ctx": 16384, "num_predict": 2048}}
