2. Be trained in the safe handling of hazardous materials and be able to demonstrate proficiency in the safe handling of hazardous materials.

3. Have access to appropriate safety equipment, including personal protective equipment (PPE), fire extinguishers, and emergency response equipment.

4. Keep accurate records of all transportation activities involving hazardous materials, including the date, time, location, type of cargo, quantity of cargo, mode of transport, driver's name, driver's license number, driver's contact information, and any other relevant information.
