2026-10-17 08:57:31,140 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=If your vehicle catches fire while you are driving, the first thing to do is to stop the vehicle as soon as possible. Once the vehicle has stopped, the next step is to extinguish the fire in the vehicle. This can be done by using a fire extinguisher on the fire in the vehicle. It is important to note that if the fire in the vehicle is too large for the fire extinguisher to effectively extinguish the fire, then it may be necessary to use other methods to extinguish the fire in the vehicle.
