on: Judgement and self control are affected by A) a high blood alcohol (BAC), B) the duration of the trip, C) inclement weather and hazardous road conditions, D) the number of years of experience a driver has?\nExcerpt: As your blood alcohol concentration (BAC) goes up, the first thing to be impaired is your judgement and selfcontrol, both of which are necessary in order to be a good driver.\n\n[5] Question: Before taking a trip, you need to inspect your tires.  Which of the following problems would require immediate action? A) a 4/32 inch tread depth on front tires, B) valve steps have been cut, C) tread separation, D) no fabric is visible through the tread or sidewall?\nExcerpt: If your tire shows tread separation, which is when the tread of the tire pulls away from the tire's casing, you should immediately take steps to find a new, more suitable tire.\n</sources>\nQuestion: During an emergency braking situation, skidding tires means?"}], "stream": true, "options": {"temperature": 0.2, "num_ctx": 16384, "num_predict": 2048}}
