2026-10-17 10:46:15,165 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=be equipped with a hydraulic braking system (HBS) or a pneumatic braking system (PBS). The HBS uses a pressurized fluid to generate force on the brakes. The PBS uses compressed air to generate force on the brakes. In both systems, there are typically two types of brakes: the "service brake" which is used when you need to slow down your vehicle, and the "traction brake" which is used when you need to stop your vehicle immediately, without any chance for it to continue moving.

In order to perform an air brake leakage test, the vehicle must be equipped with a hydraulic braking system (HBS) or a pneumatic braking system (PBS). The HBS uses a pressurized fluid to generate force on the brakes. The PBS uses compressed air to generate force on the brakes.
