oad is slippery, avoid using the engine’s braking effect and speed retarders. These can lead to wheel skids, which can be very dangerous.\n\n[5] Question: If driving emergency forces you to leave the road at any time, which of the following strategies will help you,  avoid using your brakes until you've dropped your speed to about 30 mph, if possible keep all four wheels on the same type of ground material whether road or dirt, avoid the shoulder of road which often contains debris and other potential hazards or use only light pressure on your brakes to avoid skidding on loose surfaces?\nExcerpt: only use light pressure on your breaks to avoid skidding on loose surfaces\n</sources>\nQuestion: To avoid mechanical damage, it's important to"}], "stream": true, "options": {"temperature": 0.2, "num_ctx": 16384, "num_predict": 2048}}
