2026-10-17 14:13:04,743 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=To answer this question, I need to look up the term "tie-down" and see what it means in this context.
Based on my research, a tie-down is a device used to secure loads on flatbed trailers. The device consists of a loop or cable that is attached to the load and then secured to some other point on the trailer, such as a wall or post.
In order to keep the cargo from shifting, every 5 feet of cargo should have at least one tie-down. This is because the cargo will be more likely to shift if it is not being held in place by any kind of support or reinforcement.
