2026-10-17 14:16:18,727 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=The most effective plan of action to take if your vehicle catches fire while you are driving is:

1. Pull over to a safe location as soon as possible.
2. Turn off the engine and apply direct pressure to the wound in an attempt to smother the flames.
3. If necessary, use non-conductive agents such as carbon dioxide or dry chemicals to extinguish the flames.
4. Once the flames are extinguished, continue driving to the nearest emergency services facility for further assistance.

Note: The above plan of action is based on general knowledge and may not be applicable in all situations. It is always recommended to consult with an experienced professional in the field of vehicle safety and emergency response for more accurate and tailored advice.
