2026-10-18 10:11:20,411 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=Brake fade occurs when the brakes are applied and the wheels lock up, but the brake pads do not receive enough heat to maintain their effectiveness. This can result in a reduced stopping distance, increased stopping time, or both. It is important to regularly inspect and maintain the brakes on your vehicle to prevent brake fade and other issues.
