2026-10-18 10:21:05,729 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=The holding mechanism for spring brakes released during normal driving is the spring itself. The spring acts as a shock absorber, helping to dampen the sudden release of spring brakes. This helps to prevent damage to the vehicle or its components.
