2026-10-18 10:22:54,181 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=The purpose of an antilock braking system, or ABS, is to provide a safer and more efficient way of stopping vehicles. ABS works by detecting when a vehicle's wheels are about to lock up due to over-braking. When this occurs, the ABS system applies hydraulic pressure to the brake calipers, which in turn apply hydraulic pressure to the brake pads. This results in the brakes being applied more evenly and effectively, thereby reducing the risk of wheel lock-up and other related issues.
