2026-10-18 10:31:35,300 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=No, the train's horn is not a reliable way to determine whether a crossing is clear. The train's horn is only used when the train is approaching the crossing and it needs to sound its horn in order to warn people of the approaching train. However, even if the train's horn is sounded at the crossing, it does not guarantee that the crossing is clear. There may be other obstacles or hazards that need to be taken into account in order to determine whether a crossing is clear.
