2026-10-18 10:32:08,221 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=Raising railroad crossings can be dangerous for low-clearance trailers because it increases the distance between the vehicle's center of gravity and the tracks, which can increase the risk of a collision.
Additionally, raising railroad crossings can also make it more difficult for emergency responders to access the tracks in case of an emergency.
