2026-10-18 10:42:57,068 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=A driver should avoid driving through deep standing water because it can be dangerous for the driver and other road users.
Driving through deep standing water can cause the vehicle to become unstable, which can lead to the vehicle tipping over or sinking into the water.
In addition to being dangerous for the driver and other road users, driving through deep standing water can also cause damage to the vehicle itself.
For these reasons, it is important for drivers to avoid driving through deep standing water.
