2026-10-18 10:43:11,934 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=A driver should avoid driving through deep standing water because it can be dangerous for both the driver and any passengers in the vehicle.
Deep standing water can create an unstable surface for vehicles to drive on, which can lead to skidding or other types of vehicle instability.
In addition to the potential for vehicle instability, deep standing water can also pose a risk to the safety of the driver and any passengers in the vehicle.
Therefore, it is important for drivers to be aware of the potential risks associated with driving through deep standing water.
