2026-10-18 11:00:05,105 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=Yes, a truck can meet its total weight limit while exceeding an axle weight limit. This occurs when the additional weight is distributed evenly across all axles of the truck. In this case, the total weight limit of the truck (80,000 pounds)) is not exceeded by the additional weight (e.g., cargo piled up high) which is distributed evenly across all axles of the truck.
