2026-10-18 11:07:49,637 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=If there is oil or grease on brake linings, it can cause several issues:

1. Reduced braking effectiveness: The grease or oil can reduce the friction between the brake lining and the drum or disk. This can result in a reduced braking effectiveness.

2. Increased risk of accidents: If the grease or oil on the brake linings is not cleaned promptly, it can accumulate over time. This accumulation of grease or oil on the brake linings can increase the risk of accidents by reducing the friction between the brake lining and the drum or disk.
