2026-10-18 11:08:27,326 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=The brake slack adjuster is a device used in air brakes systems to control the slack or difference between the actual and desired pressures.
During normal operation, the actual pressure of the air brakes system will be slightly higher than the desired pressure. This difference between the actual and desired pressures is called "slack" or "difference".
To control this slack or difference between the actual and desired pressures, brake slack adjusters are used in air brakes systems.
During normal operation, the brake Slack Adjuster will be adjusted to a certain value. This value of the brake Slack Adjuster will be determined by the manufacturer of the air brakes system.
