2026-10-18 12:17:32,836 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=Liquid surge occurs when the liquid inside a container or tank suddenly surges outward due to an imbalance in the liquid's density. This can happen if there is not enough liquid in the container or tank, causing it to become more dense than the surrounding liquid. As a result of this imbalance in the liquid's density, the liquid inside the container or tank suddenly surges outward due to this imbalance in the liquid's density.
