2026-10-18 12:17:46,605 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=Liquid surge occurs when a liquid tanker experiences a sudden increase in pressure inside the tanker.
This increase in pressure can be caused by a number of factors, including the sudden release of air from inside the tanker, or the sudden increase in temperature inside the tanker.
Regardless of the cause, liquid surge can result in a significant increase in pressure inside the tanker, potentially resulting in damage to the tanker or its contents.
