2026-10-18 12:29:14,690 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=The reason why a tank can reach its weight limit before reaching its volume capacity is due to the different ways that weight and volume are measured in a tank.
Weight is typically measured by subtracting the weight of the empty tank from the weight of the full tank. This method of measuring weight assumes that the density of the liquid in the tank remains constant throughout the entire process of filling or emptying the tank.
