2026-10-18 14:46:09,079 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=The number of button presses required to initiate or terminate a permitted hands-free call depends on the specific device and its user interface.
In general, modern smartphones and other mobile devices that support hands-free calling typically have a touch screen or other input mechanism that allows users to interact with their devices using a variety of gestures, including tapping, swiping, pinching, and more.
The exact number of button presses required to initiate or terminate a permitted hands-free call depends on the specific device and its user interface.
