2026-10-18 14:50:22,442 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=Children should never walk behind a school bus because it poses a safety risk to both the child and the driver of the school bus.
When a child walks behind a school bus, they are essentially standing directly in front of the driver of the school bus. This creates a situation where the driver of the school bus cannot see the child walking behind the school bus. This can create a situation where the child is at risk of being hit by debris if another vehicle collides with the bus.
In order to prevent situations like this from occurring, children should never walk behind a school bus. Instead, children should always walk in front of a school bus.
