2026-10-18 14:55:41,337 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=Yes, resurfacing a roadway can reduce clearance beneath a bridge. This is because when a road surface is resurfaced, it may not have been properly compacted or leveled before the new surface was installed. As a result, there may be some residual gaps or voids beneath the new road surface that were not properly filled or compensated for before the new surface was installed. These residual gaps or voids beneath the new road surface may cause some residual clearance beneath the bridge that was not properly filled or compensated for before the new road surface was installed.
