2026-10-18 15:03:58,769 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=Controlled braking, also known as controlled or stab braking, refers to an emergency braking technique used by drivers when they encounter a situation where their vehicle's wheels lock up. In this case, the driver will apply brakes all the way and release when the wheels lock up in order to ensure that their vehicle can continue travelling in a straight line and allow them to turn if they need to.
