2026-10-18 15:05:00,159 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=To correct an acceleration skid, a driver should:

  1. Stop Braking: This will let the rear wheels roll again, and keep the rear wheels from sliding.
  2. Counter-Steer: As a vehicle turns back on course, it has a tendency to keep on turning. Unless you turn the steering wheel quickly the other way, you may find yourself skidding in the opposite direction.
  3. Learn to Stay Off the Brake, Turn the Steering Wheel Quickly, Push in the Clutch, and Counter-Steer in a Skid Takes a Lot of Practice
