2026-10-18 15:05:12,598 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=To correct an acceleration skid, a driver should:

  1. Stop accelerating.
  2. Counter-steer in the opposite direction of the skid.
  3. If the wheels are still skidding after counter-steering, then the driver should continue to brake and counter-steer until the wheels stop skidding.

It is important to note that this information may not be up-to-date or accurate, and it should not be relied upon as the sole basis for any decision or action.
