ty quickly.\n\n[4] Question: It is important to empty the compressed air tank because oil and water collect there. If you don't have an automatic tank, you should empty your tank  how often ?\nExcerpt: It’s harmful for the air compressor tank to have water and oil in it. For example, if temperatures are below freezing, it can freeze the water and cause brake failure. If you don't have an automatic drain valve, make sure to empty your tank at the end of each driving day.\n\n[5] Question: If your vehicle has overheated and you need to remove the radiator cap, you can tell that it's cool enough to open if\nExcerpt: You can touch the cap with your bare hand without injury!  If your vehicle has overheated, it's important to never remove the radiator cap if you have a pressurized system. This can cause severe injury. If the cap is cool to the touch, it's probably safe to remove the cap.\n</sources>\nQuestion: What does an air dryer remove?"}], "stream": true, "options": {"temperature": 0.2, "num_ctx": 16384, "num_predict": 2048}}
