2026-10-18 15:26:07,666 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=A subsidiary hazard is a potential risk that is not directly related to the primary hazard, but could arise if the primary hazard were to occur. For example, if there was an explosion caused by a gas leak, and this gas leak was considered to be a primary hazard, then any subsequent fire or other damage caused by the gas leak would be considered as a subsidiary hazard.
