2026-10-18 15:37:30,763 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=If you are on a curve and need to place safety triangles, the distance needed to be placed will depend on various factors such as the curvature of the road, the speed at which you are driving, and the type of safety triangle that you are using.
In general, it is recommended to place safety triangles at least 10 feet away from your vehicle in both directions or on an undivided highway. However, depending on the specific circumstances and requirements of the applicable laws and regulations, it may be necessary to place safety triangles at a greater distance than 10 feet away from your vehicle in both directions or on an undivided highway.
