2026-10-18 15:51:56,518 INFO backend.app: llm final response topic=CDLA text=The answer to your question is that a fully loaded semitrailer will stop more slowly than an empty semitrailer, which will stop even more slowly than a fully loaded semitrailer. This is because the weight of the semitrailer increases as it becomes fuller, and this increased weight causes the semitrailer to slow down more gradually as its weight increases.
