ached to the \nlines with the words \"service\" and \"emergency\" \nstamped on them. See Figure 6.6 \n \n \nFigure 6.6\n\n[4] Question: What is the Emergency Response Guidebook used for?\nExcerpt: The Emergency Response Guidebook (ERG) is a publication developed by the U.S. Department of Transportation's Federal Highway Administration (FHWA). The ERG serves as a reference guide for emergency responders, including firefighters, police officers, and other first responders.\n\nThe ERG provides detailed information on various types of emergencies, including natural disasters such as hurricanes, earthquakes, and tornadoes; man-made disasters such as industrial accidents, chemical spills, and nuclear accidents; transportation-related emergencies such as vehicle breakdowns, tire blowouts, and engine failures; and medical emergency situations such as heart attacks, strokes, and other serious medical conditions.\n\nThe ERG is designed to be comprehensive, easy-to-read, and up-to-date with the latest information on various types of emergencies.\n\n[5] Question: CDLA\nExcerpt: check the vehicle’s position while \nbacking. You may be permitted to safely stop and \nexit the vehicle to check the external position of the \nvehicle (look).  \nWhen doing so, you must set the parking brake(s) \nand place the vehicle in neutral/park. Then, when \nexiting/entering the vehicle, you must do so safely \nby facing the vehicle and maintaining three (3) \npoints of contact with the vehicle at all times (when \nexiting/entering a bus, you may face forward and \nmaintain a firm grasp on the handrail). If you do not \nsafely secure the vehicle or safely exit/enter the \nvehicle, it may result in an automatic failure for an \nunsafe act.   \nIf you open your door or move from a seated \nposition, it will count as a \"look.” If you open your \ndoor while the vehicle is moving (not in neutral and \npark), it may result in an automatic failure for an \nunsafe act.  \nOn a bus, if you walk to the back \n</sources>\nQuestion: Hello"}], "stream": true, "options": {"temperature": 0.2, "num_ctx": 16384, "num_predict": 2048}}
